---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '../components/layout/Container.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout
  rawTitle="About This Free Webcam Test Site"
  description="About Webcam Test, a fast, free, privacy-first tool to check your camera and microphone directly in your browser."
>
  <Container class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="caption-mono uppercase text-mute">About</p>
      <h1 class="display-xl mt-3 text-ink">A webcam test that respects you.</h1>
      <p class="body-lg mt-6 text-body">
        {SITE.name} is a free tool for confirming that your camera and microphone work before an
        important call, interview, or stream. It is built to be fast, honest, and completely
        private no account, no download, and nothing uploaded.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-12 text-ink">Why it exists</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        The usual way to check a camera is to join a call early and ask whether people can see
        you. That works, but it puts you on display while you fiddle with settings, and it tells
        you nothing about why the picture looks poor. Meanwhile most “webcam test” sites bury a
        small preview under advertising, and a few ask you to install something first for a
        task the browser can already do on its own.
      </p>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        This site takes the opposite approach. The preview is the largest thing on the page, the
        measurements are real, and the whole check is over in about a minute.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">How it works</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        The test uses standard browser APIs <span class="code-font">getUserMedia</span> for the
        camera and the Web Audio API for the microphone, to access your devices{' '}
        <em>locally</em>. Your browser asks for permission, streams the feed to a preview on this
        page, and every measurement is computed on your device from frames that never travel
        anywhere. It is the same mechanism your video-conferencing app uses, with nothing sitting
        between you and the result.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">What makes it different</h2>
      <ul class="body-md mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 ps-5 text-body">
        <li>Live-measured frame rate and bitrate, counted from real frames rather than the spec sheet.</li>
        <li>Record a few seconds and play it back, because a mirror preview hides what a call shows.</li>
        <li>Camera, microphone <em>and</em> speakers in one place, plus focused tools for each dimension.</li>
        <li>Rule-of-thirds framing guides, so you can fix your framing rather than guess at it.</li>
        <li>Automatic health checks that flag a problem and tell you how to fix it.</li>
        <li>A one-click diagnostics report to paste into a support ticket.</li>
        <li>A troubleshooting guide with the exact settings path for each browser and OS.</li>
        <li>No ads over your preview, no account, no downloads, no dark patterns.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Who it is for</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        Anyone about to be seen on camera: candidates before an interview, teachers before a
        lesson, clinicians before a telehealth appointment, streamers checking a new setup, and
        support teams who need to walk someone else through a camera problem over the phone.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Privacy</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        Your video and audio never leave your device. There is no server that receives your feed
        and no way for us to see it. The full detail is on our{' '}
        <a class="text-link hover:text-link-deep" href="/privacy">privacy page</a>, and the{' '}
        <a class="text-link hover:text-link-deep" href="/terms">terms of use</a> cover the rest.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Get in touch</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        Found a bug, or a camera that behaves strangely? Tell us at{' '}
        <a class="text-link hover:text-link-deep" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, or
        see the <a class="text-link hover:text-link-deep" href="/contact">contact page</a>.
        Reports that include your browser, operating system and camera model are the most useful.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
